[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Mr Odd Ball
GenericName=Character face
Comment=His animated face. Escape leaves fullscreen, Ctrl+Q quits, F11 toggles.
Categories=Utility;

# Absolute paths, NOT %h. Desktop entries expand %f %F %u %U %i %c %k and nothing else —
# systemd's %h means nothing here and would be passed through as the literal string, so the
# window would fail to start with a path that does not exist.
#
# The URL is QUOTED, and that is not cosmetic. The Desktop Entry spec lists "?" among the
# reserved characters an Exec argument may not carry unquoted — an unquoted `?solo=1` is
# malformed, and a launcher is free to mangle or reject the whole line. It would fail as
# "his face didn't come up after a reboot", days later, with nothing pointing here.
Exec=/home/ironi/oddball/venv/bin/python /home/ironi/oddball/hud/float.py --url "http://127.0.0.1:8765/?chat=1" --transparent --undecorated --width 1100 --height 620
Path=/home/ironi/oddball
Icon=/home/ironi/oddball/assets/mr-odd-ball-reference.png

Terminal=false
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true

# No ordering against oddball.service on purpose. The rig retries its WebSocket every 2s
# forever and shows his resting state until it connects, so it does not matter which of the two
# starts first — and that is a property of the rig worth keeping rather than designing around.
#
# ?chat=1 rather than ?solo=1, since 2026-08-19. He is the EE copilot now, and a firmware
# answer contains a C snippet and a register table — D32 measured Piper at ~160 wpm, so 40
# words is about 15 seconds of audio and none of that can be read aloud. engine/split.py sends
# the sentence to his mouth and everything else to the panel beside him, so the panel has to
# be on screen or half of every answer is lost.
#
# For him alone with no panel — the look D41 shipped — put ?solo=1 back and use
# --width 600 --height 600. Nothing else changes; both are modes of the same rig.
#
# Three flags make the transparency work, and all three are required — drop any one and the
# effect disappears completely rather than degrading:
#
#   ?chat=1        the page hides its dev chrome and clears its background
#   --transparent  the window paints no backdrop either
#   --undecorated  no title bar, which is a backdrop with a name on it
#
# 1100x620 rather than fullscreen, deliberately. Fullscreen + transparent is an invisible
# window covering the whole display that still swallows every click: the desktop would look
# reachable and not be. It is wider than the old 600x600 because he now shares the window —
# the rig gives him 42% and the panel the rest, and a chat column under ~600px wraps a
# register table into nonsense.
#
# Wayland lets no client place its own window, so labwc decides where he lands. There is no
# title bar to drag him by; Super+drag moves him. Anchoring him to a corner needs
# gtk4-layer-shell, which is NOT installed — the Pi has libgtk-layer-shell0 0.9.0-2, the GTK3
# build, which cannot load into this GTK4 process.
#
# THE WAY OUT, since there is no close button: Escape closes a windowed face, Ctrl+Q always
# quits. Both need keyboard focus — click him first.
#
# For the old fullscreen look on a solid backdrop, drop `--transparent --undecorated --width
# 600 --height 600` and add `--fullscreen`. For the development page with all its buttons,
# drop `?solo=1` too.
#
# This ran tools/spike_gtk_face.py until 2026-08-19, and this comment used to say that when
# the chat application existed, this Exec line was the one thing that would have to change.
# It existed, and it was — the spike is now hud/float.py and the URL carries ?chat=1. Nothing
# inside the window needed changing at all, which is what ?chat=1 being a mode of the same rig
# rather than a second page bought.
